  "notes": "West leads the ♠K against 5♥. After East overtakes West's ♠K and returns the suit, South has a decision to make. East has shown 8 spades and West is likely to have the ♥Q. In that case, if South ruffs low, West will be able to overruff. The contract will probably fail if diamonds are 4-1.\n\nSouth should ruff with the ♥A and finesse West for the ♥Q. East's discard means that there is still a trump loser. South should now cash 2 top diamonds. When East discards again the contract seems to be in trouble.\n\nSouth now has a complete count on the hand (East is 8014) and he can succeed with a smother play, denying West his natural trump trick. South continues with 3 rounds of clubs, ruffing the third round. South's trumps have been shortened to the same number as West's.\n\nSouth finesses again in hearts. Next he cashes dummy's third diamond winner and leads North's remaining spade discarding South's diamond loser. West must also discard. East has only black cards left and will smother his partner's ♥Q whatever he returns.",
